# The house at twice the density (plan §4.7, §10 G9): 96x96 on a 48 px grid, the same 2x2-cell
# footprint. Started as a nearest-neighbour scale-up of the 1x house, then detailed where 2x has
# room the 1x copy has not: courses of roof tiles, the plaster's texture, the door's planks and
# the window glazing bars. The density check reduces it back and compares it with the 1x house.
fork house house_2x
scale 2
density of=house d=2

# --- courses of roof tiles: a darker line every fourth row on the roof's middle tones
select colour c=roof2
select colour c=roof1 add
line 0,10 95,10 c=roof1
line 0,18 95,18 c=roof1
line 0,26 95,26 c=roof1
line 0,34 95,34 c=roof1
line 0,42 95,42 c=roof1
deselect
# --- plaster texture: a few flecks of the wall's shade
select colour c=wall1
px 15,57 16,57 33,60 58,56 59,56 70,61 77,58 13,79 30,82 31,82 62,80 75,84 76,84 c=wall0
deselect
# --- the door's planks split again, the glazing bars thinner
line 47,66 47,87 c=wood1
line 53,66 53,87 c=wood1
